  "title": "Builder-family detection, fail-closed reviews, and diff-aware posting",
  "summary": "This change reworks how osf decides which model family built a reviewed range, and what happens when it cannot tell. Family detection now scans every word of a Code-Generator trailer (vendor names and model ids alike) and reports why a family is unknown; a clean merge with no trailer is exempt via a read-only git merge-tree check. An unknown builder family now fails the run closed: no reviewer counts, the outcome is could-not-run, and each reviewer's saved run records why it sat out. Separately, review posting now fetches the pull request diff, keeps inline comments only on lines the diff shows, moves the rest into the body, and cuts rather than refuses an over-long body.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
